Database created and seeded
2_Funds_parser/2_fundparser.db now contains one table, funds, with 22 rows — every selected fund from column A of your Excel, paired with its legal name and 10-digit CIK.

Files produced
src/database/schema.sql — funds(id, cik UNIQUE, name, legal_name, created_at, updated_at) + idx_funds_name.
src/database/db.py — get_connection() resolves 2_fundparser.db at the project root and applies schema.sql idempotently on every connect; also exports now_iso().
src/database/init.py — empty.
scripts/2_seed_funds.py — reads Input/list_of_funds.xlsx sheet "Confirmed Funds", keeps rows with non-empty column A, upserts by CIK. Re-runnable; refreshes name/legal_name on conflict.
spec/2_layer_0.md — the Layer 0 spec (fund registry only; no tiers/multipliers/policy columns — deliberate simplification vs 1_Stock_Picker).
